p5-style instrument (carrier as bit count): extents mapping to more than one carrier value: 0

p5's own model conflates `native_p5_style` with 128 for every width above 64,
so at W = 249..768 it reports a UNIFORM carrier bit count of 128 for Hot, Warm
and Precise alike, never distinguishing the wide-rung align-16 case from the
align-1 case at all, because its representation of a carrier is a number, not
a type, and its own model of `native` never grows past 128 in the first place.

p1's type-aware instrument, same domain, found: 40 of 640 real collisions.
this instrument, reproducing p5's own representation on the same domain: 0.

0 versus 40 on the identical (W, strategy) domain is not a disagreement about facts;
it is p5's own carrier representation being unable to express the fact that would
refute its claim. this is the same blindness `16` itself diagnosed in section 5
for the erasure-and-codegen-equality check ("its instrument is a scalar... a
carrier-only derivation passes it at full marks"), now found in `16`'s OWN
instrument for the pair's irreducibility claim, in the same file.
